\begin{appendices}

\section{Test Scenario Details}\label{secA1}

The ``Lost in Conversation'' test scenario adapts the methodology from Liu et al.~\cite{liu2023lostinthemiddle} to multi-turn dialogue. Four HumanEval coding problems are sharded and interleaved across 40+ conversation turns, with each problem discussed in 8--12 non-contiguous segments.

The scenario tests whether the system can correctly identify which problem is being discussed based on:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Subchat context (for Conversation Forests)
    \item Linear position and RAG retrieval (for baseline)
\end{enumerate}

Each response is evaluated for correct topic identification using an LLM-based classifier that checks whether the response addresses the intended problem rather than confusing it with semantically similar alternatives.

\end{appendices}

